# ASUS ProArt PX13 (HN7306) - keep the rt721-sdca jack codec out of runtime suspend.
#
# NOT installed by install-durable.sh in this fork: the failure below did not
# reproduce on linux-omarchy 7.2.5 (2026-09-16 - rt721 runtime-suspended ~5 s
# after boot and resumed cleanly when the jack PCM was opened). Kept ready for
# a kernel where it does; check-audio.sh names it when the symptom appears.
#
# Seen upstream (ftoleedo/px13-audio-fix cde590d) on kernel 7.3.0-rc2: the
# codec runtime-suspends ~7 s after probe and never comes back:
# rt721_sdca_dev_resume() -> regcache_sync() fails with -ENODATA (-61), i.e.
# the peripheral ignores the bus writes although sysfs still says "Attached".
# Every later pm_runtime_get() fails the same way, so the
# SDW1-PIN0-PLAYBACK-SimpleJack PCM cannot open. PipeWire's ACP needs every
# mapping of the UCM HiFi verb to probe, so the dead Headphones mapping drops
# the whole profile and takes the internal Speaker down with it - the card is
# left offering only 'off' and 'pro-audio', with no speaker sink at all.
#
# Forbidding runtime PM at device-add time means the first suspend never
# happens, so the broken resume path is never taken. Cost: the jack codec stays
# powered (milliwatts). Remove once the resume works upstream again.
#
# Install:
#   sudo install -Dm644 configs/90-px13-rt721-no-autosuspend.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/
#   sudo udevadm control --reload
#   for d in /sys/bus/soundwire/devices/sdw:*:025d:0721:*; do echo on | sudo tee $d/power/control; done
#   sudo /usr/local/lib/px13-soundwire-recover.sh     # if the speaker sink is already gone
# (policy auto may see a healthy bus - use PX13_RECOVER_POLICY=always then)
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="soundwire", KERNEL=="sdw:*:025d:0721:*", ATTR{power/control}="on"
